{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our sales-insights agent (ADK, gemini-2.5-pro) keeps generating SQL that references columns that don't exist — like it'll do `SELECT region_name FROM orders` when the column is `region_cd` and you have to join dim_region. Right now I'm just dumping INFORMATION_SCHEMA for the whole `analytics_prod` dataset into the system instruction, which is like 40k tokens and honestly I think it's making things worse. How should I be feeding schema to the model instead? Maybe only pull the relevant tables per question? Demo to the CFO's team is Thursday so something pragmatic please."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Need to lock down the BigQuery tool in our NL-to-SQL agent. Requirements from security: (1) agent can only ever run SELECTs, no DML/DDL even if the model gets prompt-injected, (2) dedicated service account with minimum roles on just the reporting dataset, (3) teardown script that removes the SA and IAM bindings when we decommission an environment. Currently it runs as the default compute SA which I know is bad. Also want to keep a library of vetted query templates the agent prefers over freeform SQL. What's the cleanest way to do all of this?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "ugh. our scheduled BigQuery job that builds the daily_revenue table (the one our query agent reads from) has been timing out since we added the new partitions last week. it's a big MERGE with like 6 CTEs and the slot usage looks insane in the console. can you help me figure out why it's so slow and rewrite it?", "needs_instead": "This is BigQuery performance tuning for a batch ETL/MERGE job (partitioning, clustering, query plan, slot usage), not help with the natural-language query agent itself."}
]}
